{'name': 'Mexican Fresh', 'address': '315 Meigs Rd, Ste F', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Mexican, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-03-03 03:37:40', 'review_text': 'Below average. I run errands in this plaza so I stopped in for a burrito. The place screams "clean me." Everything looks tired and dirty. The cashier was ill with a cold. The cook kept telling her not to "talk to me like that. Ever." 

Seemed like a family feud. The young son was chewing on something in front of a TV. wasn't he supposed to be in school?

Burrito was a good size but chicken was a bit chewy and dry. The atmosphere scared me so I won't be going back.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2016-01-19 21:20:25', 'review_text': 'The carnitas is very good, burritos are huge! Good food at a reasonable price. Great salsa selection to go with whatever you order.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2015-12-30 06:18:29', 'review_text': '3.5 stars is accurate. Good, affordable, and fast Mexican food. Love the salsa bar with containers to go!'}]}

{'name': 'Pacific Crêpes', 'address': '705 Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Wine Bars, Restaurants, Gluten-Free, French, Bars, Nightlife, Creperies', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-15:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-15:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-15:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-15:0', 'Friday': '10:0-15:0', 'Saturday': '9:0-15:0', 'Sunday': '9:0-15:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-09-21 13:12:45', 'review_text': 'All their salads are good but my daughter and I loved the Monaco and Celtic salad the best,  and they also have a lot of choices for crepes. Great food, good customer service and reasonable price...I will definitely recommend this place! Keep it up, Pacific Crepes!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-02-17 21:29:46', 'review_text': "We will miss Pacific Crêpes. They were the real thing. The owners were from Brittany, France. When the mother worked there she ONLY spoke French, even if the customers couldn't. I still don't know how much English she could speak. They hosted our French conversation group for many years (we now meet Wednesdays at Arnoldi's; if you speak a little français come join us). Au revoir, PC!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-11-26 06:51:57', 'review_text': 'Delicious and unique french cafe.  Wonderful service.  Amazing coffee too.  Try coffee Mocca.

Enjoy!

We will be back!'}]}

{'name': 'Santa Barbara Harbor & Seafood Festival', 'address': '141-153 Harbor Way', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Local Flavor, Seafood, Arts & Entertainment, Shopping, Festivals, Restaurants, Arts & Crafts', 'hours': {'Saturday': '10:0-17:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-09-08 22:31:44', 'review_text': "Beach shack for takeout on one side and casual dine-in restaurant on the other side.  We had the ceviche, albacore tuna melt and ahi tacos. All were very good and we'd get them again! Ordered the bartender special cocktail - good but a little pricey and served in a martini glass so not a lot of cocktail.  All in all, a fun place with decent food."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-10-15 00:23:03', 'review_text': "We flew to LAX 1 day before, and drove 2 hours from LA to Santa Barbara which is our trip main itinerary. There are several tents selling merchandise along from parking lot to pier. On the pier, you can get fresh sea urchin, crabs, and spiky lobsters. Lobsters each weighs over 1 lb to almost 2 lbs. You just hand picked and paid by the weight which they accept credit card. Then you proceed to cook station for fee of $5 and waited for about an hour. We also got a plate of paella, a cup of clam chowder for our lunch. Initially wanted to try fresh oysters a dozen for $25 but the line was too long. There's ceviche, taco, street corn, etc. Once we got our food, we settled down near the beach picnic table under palm trees. 

All and all, the experience was great. Enjoyed driving along beach despite the LA traffic."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2019-10-14 01:18:58', 'review_text': 'Over crowded festival with overpriced food. I was mainly interested in tasting some fresh uni.  There were a couple of venders selling live uni but most of them had hardly any eggs in it.  I paid one for $15 and it was okay but not good enough to get another one.  The live fish and lobsters, after purchasing them, you have to take them to a different tent to cook for you and there was a long line.  I had to wait for 30 minutes for jambalaya shrimp which had four little shrimp and the rest was rice.   And it was too salty. Seafood paella looked good but again there was a long line.  Overall, I was very disappointed.  There was nothing special about this festival.  I can have live lobsters or crab at home anytime for much less price.  
.'}]}

{'name': 'On the Side', 'address': '6521 Pardall Rd', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (Traditional), Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2010-08-04 21:32:49', 'review_text': "Meh.

Granted, as a vegetarian I may not be the intended diner of OTS. That being said, I've been a couple times with different omnivorous friends who have ranging impressions of the place. While some of my friends seem to like it, many seemed underwhelmed by the wings, their staple item. I've gotten the artichoke hearts a couple times, which are decent, but offensively overpriced. This seems to be the moral of On the Side's story.

Possibly the place's saving grace is their great selection of brews. Unfortunately, their selection comes with a price. They have a bunch of flat screens, so I'd say this is a good place to grab a drink and watch a game, but I wouldn't recommend it much further than that."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2010-07-15 17:47:10', 'review_text': 'They changed the way you order which is TOTAL CRAP!!! Instead of resteraunt style ordering everyone has to order up at the counter now which is just ridiculous. They need to change this back again ASAP!'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-06-24 00:21:25', 'review_text': 'Good food. The portions looked kinda small at first, but was full by the time I finished everything. My favorite item is the buffalo wings, they might be some of the best in santa barbara. The service was like whatevers, the waitress was kind of a noob and forgot about taking back the bill so i had to go up to the counter and pay there.'}]}

{'name': 'State & A Bar and Grill', 'address': '1201 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Restaurants, Nightlife, Barbeque', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-07-17 01:38:31', 'review_text': 'Flashback!  My old happy hour spot. Great outdoor patio. Glad I got one last visit in. They are closed now and new restaurant is on the way.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-14 14:12:39', 'review_text': 'food was good, maybe a little over priced, but what they lacked in quality they made up for in customer service.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2011-04-13 11:15:00', 'review_text': "I seriously thought I was on candid camera or something.  I came in for a late lunch one day and everything I got here was absolutely wretched...even their drinks!

Its such a shame because they have a great location and a nice outdoor patio...how do they stay in business??

I must say this place also gets an award: the absolute worst calamari I've ever sampled in my life (and that's saying something)."}]}

{'name': 'Left At Albuquerque', 'address': '700 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Tex-Mex, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-01-13 20:29:31', 'review_text': 'Was here visiting from out of town. Stayed for most of happy hour a couple days. killer margaritas. And huge selection of tequilas too. 

The reason I gave it a great review is they had an appetizer I have never been able to find anywhere else. It was called "Ball of Fire" "For people that like really hot or just plain lunatics" It was a Habanero Popper. Like a jalapeno popper but WAYYYYY hotter. It was fun trying to cool off with more beer or margaritas. Thank God we had a ride back home. Anyhow great memory & we really enjoyed the chips and salsa & the happy hours.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2009-10-05 21:23:14', 'review_text': 'It was all wrong from the moment I asked if we could sit at the bar to have an appetizer and drinks, and the girl that was seating us said, "yes," but we must order an appetizer.  Then she proceeded to take us out to the patio which confused me because I asked for the bar, but I dismissed that.  She sat us at a table, and we ordered our appetizer and drinks from the server.  He comes back with our drinks and explains that they may ask us to move inside because the patio is reserved for customers ordering dinners rather than just appetizers and drinks.  The patio was not full at all, and we told him we were told that we could order an appetizer alone, but still he said we may have to move later as that is the rule.  No apologies at all.  Ugh - I wanted to leave right after his comment...but I figured I should have my beer first.   First, we never asked to be seated outside; second, if that is a rule at the restaurant, why did they seat us outside when we specifically asked for the bar and told the seater that we were only ordering appetizer and drinks?  

Oh, the appetizer was not so great, but we didn't order anything fancy.  It's possible their other food is really good though.  The server spilled my beer on my sunglasses :( .  We quickly had our drinks and appetizer, paid, then got out of there.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2009-09-23 21:14:27', 'review_text': 'Great outdoor patio area.  Loved the ambiance.  The chips and salsa are good, food was okay.  Nothing special.'}]}

{'name': 'Kogilicious', 'address': '956 Embarcadero Del Norte', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Korean, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-23:0', 'Friday': '10:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-12-31 04:01:57', 'review_text': "Half and half beef ribs and pork FTW.  Best I've *ever* had, and I've had a lot of good Korean food."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-08-31 01:14:22', 'review_text': "So. Good. So good. A Kogilicious spicy chicken burrito is one of my favorite foods in the world. But all of the proteins are fantastic- beef, spicy pork, tofu; can't go wrong. Taco, burrito, both are great. And so reasonably priced! Pay cash; you'll get a giant burrito for less than $7, which is unheard of elsewhere in IV. This town desperately needs a proper Korean restaurant, but in the meantime, Kogilicious hits the spot."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2015-07-22 23:44:51', 'review_text': 'Three words, Spicy Pork Burrito.

Bomb.

Bring cash, they charge more if you use a card.'}]}

{'name': 'Fiesta Market & Deli', 'address': '4502 Carpinteria Ave', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Mexican, Restaurants, Grocery, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-23:0', 'Friday': '7:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-17 20:13:50', 'review_text': "Best burritos in town! Excellent customer service. If they don't carry it they will to try to order it for you."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-17 22:10:44', 'review_text': 'We stopped here with our fifth-wheel trailer. We parked a few blocks up the street.

The food was freshly made and delicious. We tried the Machaca burrito and the chicken fajitas. Best Mexican ever in Carpenteria! 

The market also stocks a huge selection of beer and wine. The cherry on top was finding our favorite Mexican beer that is difficult to find in LA.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-07-25 03:55:43', 'review_text': 'Woww my friend recommended lunch from this place and honestly it just might be my new favorite spot in town! We shared nachos and a torta and the torta was literally the same size as a Costco chicken bake. I was literally expecting it to be half of that size. My order came out to $21 and this could have easily fed 3 people, so you definitely get your moneys worth! Wait time might take about 15-20 minutes since they are always super busy!'}]}

{'name': 'Juice Ranch', 'address': '1187 Coast Village Rd, Ste 5', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Food, Live/Raw Food, Juice Bars & Smoothies, Vegan', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '7:30-17:0', 'Wednesday': '7:30-17:0', 'Thursday': '7:30-17:0', 'Friday': '7:30-17:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-14:0', 'Sunday': '9:0-17:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 15:54:28', 'review_text': 'Went in to place an order. No one working there was wearing a mask. Asked if the people making the food wore masks. The kid said "yeah we have masks." Walked out. They don't care about keeping their customers safe. Should not be in the service business. I've been there before and liked their food but clearly never going back again.

Check out all the other "not recommended" and reported reviews on the same issue that have been hidden for their rating.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-13 03:40:09', 'review_text': 'Good high quality and fresh ingredients just expensive and tiny portions. Never have I ever paid $12 for a bagel with mostly raw ingredients. 

Bowls are literally a jar of chia seeds with the least amount of toppings and flavor ever.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-17 16:44:33', 'review_text': "I like their products but I just had a very unpleasant conversation with one of the employees about masks. None of the employees need to wear masks and the one I spoke to shared that he was not vaccinated. He told me he had had COVID and wasn't afraid of COVID. I am. I've had friends die of this disease. I have friends who work in hospitals and witness the toll it has taken. There is less danger of transmission when people wear masks, so why won't this business take this step to look out doe its customers?"}]}

{'name': "Carl's Jr", 'address': '7 S Milpas St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Burgers, Fast Food, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-22:0', 'Friday': '7:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2020-06-11 18:05:33', 'review_text': "The food is what you expect from Carl's Jr.  Tasty but way too salty. 

I think the drink guy might be speaking English but I am not sure. I think he is refusing to give me another drink refill. Not even if I pay for it. I thought I was minding my business after eating lunch. I guess he is too busy with his other duties of standing around the drink machine doing nothing. 

Fortunately, McDonald's is a couple of blocks north and Habit (which is actually pretty good) is a couple of blocks south, so it is not hard to find a place where people want to work."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-14 06:09:11', 'review_text': "This is one of the best Carl's jrs I've been to. The cashier was super friendly and helpful.  The food was good and the restaurant was clean. It has an old time retro vibe. My special request was done without hesitation."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2019-09-03 20:22:37', 'review_text': "its Carl's Jr, what else is there to say. the food either taste good that day or gross. staff friendly, restaurant and facilities something clean."}]}

{'name': 'Rice Garden', 'address': '1180 University Ctr, Bldg 252', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Fast Food, Caterers, Chinese, Szechuan, Event Planning & Services, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-17:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-17:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-17:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-17:0', 'Friday': '10:0-17:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'paid', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2013-06-08 01:53:14', 'review_text': 'Its a shame, this place used to be so much better last year. They had a much wider variety last year. The curry chicken tasted almost like authentic chinese, and I enjoyed the Spicy Chicken every time. They switched around the menu, but usually they had 2 very good items everyday.

Now, its pretty much the same generic items everyday. On top of that, they are almost always sold out, whether because its rush lunch hour, or its after 2 or 3 and they just give up making half the menu.

I hear its getting replaced by Yoshinoya. I am glad because I love Yoshinoya.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2013-03-07 21:26:31', 'review_text': 'I would say the food was good if I could ever have it. Every time I go to this place they are "out" of what I want, nothing on deck, just simply out. Some times when I go they tell me that things are going to be done at exactly 1pm (which may be over 30 mins away)...its especially frustrating when these should be (and probably are) the money makers for the business. Teriyaki chicken? ITS CHICKEN, why is this not in abundance?? Why does the business run out of it!??! Why is there a 50 cents extra charge for the simplest menu item??! I can't make sense of it, I won't be going back, it is simply absurd.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2012-10-05 21:11:32', 'review_text': "Best place to eat anywhere near UCSB. It's cheap, it tastes awesome, and the service is fast and good. Everything tastes fresh, unlike Panda Express. Too bad it's gone now."}]}

{'name': "Anna's Marketplace Bakery", 'address': '7018 Marketplace Dr', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Donuts, Restaurants, Bakeries, Food, Sandwiches', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '6:0-17:30', 'Wednesday': '6:0-17:30', 'Thursday': '6:0-16:0', 'Friday': '6:0-17:30', 'Saturday': '6:0-17:30', 'Sunday': '6:0-16:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-18 01:20:49', 'review_text': 'Donuts are delish, nice and light and fresh. The chocolate croissant was really good as well! They are a little more pricey than some donut shops but have really good flavor.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-01 18:44:53', 'review_text': "Happy 2022 everyone! This year will surely see me at Anna's quite a few more times. When a friend told me that a bakery close to where I live offers vegan donuts, I was psyched--I'm vegan and it's oddly difficult to find good vegan food, sweets, and drinks in this area. Checking out Anna's Bakery a few days later, I wasn't let down. 

I've sampled both the vegan glazed donut and the apple fritter, as well as the house coffee, and all were great. The donut is puffy and airy and sweet. The fritter has glorious crunchy, oily edges and a surprisingly doughy interior, complete with apple pieces and a glossy, sugary varnish. (Did you know some 'apple fritters' elsewhere don't even contain apple?) The coffee is hot and black and perfectly balances the candy-like sweetness of the baked goods. 

There's always a long line and seating is limited so be prepared. This shop also offers non-vegan donuts (the majority contain milk products, though I'm crossing my fingers for a vegan cake donut in 2022). There is also a menu of savory food. Breads and donuts and cookies are also available to go. That pink box, unmistakably brimming with tasty treats, is sure to being smiles to any gathering... especially if you have vegan friends who are so used to being left out when sweet baked goods appear."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-27 05:28:12', 'review_text': "SO friendly and donuts are always amazing. All staff, from the cashier to the owner. All lovely people. They always greet with by my name. I love to see how they interact with all customers. I am always happy to give them business as it is very well deserved. Keep up the wonderful work! Anna's has been around for a long time and has always been one of my favorites."}]}

{'name': 'Pressed', 'address': '651 Paseo Nuevo, Ste 305', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Ice Cream & Frozen Yogurt, Juice Bars & Smoothies, Convenience Stores, Vegan, Food, Health Markets, Specialty Food, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-20:0', 'Friday': '10:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-19:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': None, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-20 00:55:49', 'review_text': 'How is it that Pressed employees are always so unpleasant and unsociable! I met one nice employee my first time at this location who was from San Diego like me. She made conversation and was genuine. My other experiences have been far from this, the employees are agitated and do not make any conversation. Honestly very disappointed because this is the second location I have been to with poor customer service.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-14 16:01:47', 'review_text': 'We happened to drive through SB yesterday and were craving some good juice so we stopped by Pressed. We ordered our usual Berry Smoothies, which were delicious as always.

The only thing that prevents me from giving this location 5 stars... the staff. I walked inside and waited a bit for someone to come out from the back. It took so long that I awkwardly tried to look into the back to see if anyone was there lol. At one point I had to yell out, "hello?" to which a guy came out to help. He wasn't very friendly and seemed a bit annoyed that I came in but maybe it was just a bad day. 

